# X in a cutscene switches how it is seen (0.1.12, the owner's ask; from 0.1.18 between the two in VR only, the owner's
# ask, never to the screen): the Novalis arrival scene through his eyes (the launcher's default), X: in VR around you,
# X: through his eyes again, X: in VR, and play after the scene in first person all the same (the View row's, which X
# leaves alone: [vr-state] first_person 1), X then the map's own. No [vr-scene] line says "on a screen".
# Then VR Options by the sticks as options.sim goes, down to the ninth row, Cutscenes (In VR, from the last X), stepped
# back to Through his eyes. The [vr-scene] lines say each step; the run's vr-options.txt keeps scene_view 0 and
# launcher_scene_view 0.
